{"content":"q28.\n\n**Runners the server actually starts** (all launched from `Server.startBackgroundRunners`, `server/server.go:153-174`):\n\n- **s3presign runner** (`server/runner/s3presign/runner.go`) — started twice-over: one synchronous `RunOnce(ctx)` at boot (`server/server.go:163`), then a goroutine running `Run(s3Context)` driven by a `time.NewTicker(runnerInterval)` with `runnerInterval = 12h` (`server/runner/s3presign/runner.go:27-41`). Per-attachment work is additionally gated by data state: it skips any S3 object whose `LastPresignedTime` is still valid for the next 4 days (`runner.go:85-91`). Shutdown is via the stored `context.CancelFunc` (`server/server.go:156-159`, `stopBackgroundRunners` at :176).\n- **HTTP serve goroutine** (`server/server.go:124-128`) — not a scheduled runner; blocks on `httpServer.Serve(listener)`, event-driven by incoming connections.\n- **Shutdown wait goroutine** (`server/server.go:186`) — one-shot, triggered by `WaitGroup` completion vs. shutdown-context deadline (`shutdownTimeout = 10s`, :29).\n\n**Periodic/async goroutines started outside the server object** (same process, worth naming since they're background work):\n\n- **store cache cleanup loop** — `go c.cleanupLoop()` at `store/cache/cache.go:83`, ticker driven by `CleanupInterval`, set to 5 minutes for all three caches in `store/store.go:40-53`. Started transitively by `store.New(...)` in `cmd/memos/main.go:64`.\n- **webhook dispatch workers** — 4 goroutines in `internal/webhook/webhook.go:42-55`, driven by the `asyncPostQueue` channel (queue depth 128), not by a clock.\n- **email send workers** — 2 goroutines in `internal/email/email.go:16-18`, driven by `asyncEmailQueue`.\n- **PAT last-used writer** — fire-and-forget goroutine per authenticated request (`server/auth/authenticator.go:179-185`).\n- **SSE heartbeat** — `time.NewTicker(sseHeartbeatInterval)` at `server/router/api/v1/sse_handler.go:64`, but it is per-connection inside the request handler, not a process-level runner.\n\n**Unused scheduling infrastructure:**\n\n- `internal/scheduler` — a complete cron scheduler (cron parser, timezone support, middleware chain, graceful stop; `internal/scheduler/scheduler.go`, `parser.go`, `job.go`, `middleware.go`, documented in `doc.go`) is **never wired into the server**. The only importers are its own tests: `internal/scheduler/example_test.go:10` and `internal/scheduler/integration_test.go:13`. The code graph returns a certified zero for callers of `Scheduler.Start`. Nothing schedules jobs by cron expression in this deployment; the only real clock-driven server work is the 12h s3presign ticker.\n- `server/runner/memopayload` — the runner type is dead as a runner: certified zero callers for both `memopayload.NewRunner` and `memopayload.Runner.RunOnce`. Only its free function `RebuildMemoPayload` is used, called inline on the request path in `server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:108` and `:447`. So the bulk memo-payload backfill exists but is never started or scheduled.","iteration":14,"turn":1,"type":"assistant"}
